#: src/tasks.md:62
msgid ""
"There are two actions that drive the workflow of using tasks: `task: spawn` "
"and `task: rerun`. `task: spawn` opens a modal with all available tasks in "
"the current file. `task: rerun` reruns the most recently spawned task. You "
"can also rerun tasks from the task modal."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:66
msgid ""
"By default, rerunning tasks reuses the same terminal (due to the "
"`\"use_new_terminal\": false` default) but waits for the previous task to "
"finish before starting (due to the `\"allow_concurrent_runs\": false` "
"default)."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:68
msgid ""
"Keep `\"use_new_terminal\": false` and set `\"allow_concurrent_runs\": true` "
"to allow cancelling previous tasks on rerun."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:70
msgid "Task templates"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:72
msgid "Tasks can be defined:"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:74
msgid ""
"in the global `tasks.json` file; such tasks are available in all Zed "
"projects you work on. This file is usually located in `~/.config/zed/tasks."
"json`. You can edit them by using the `zed: open tasks` action."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:75
msgid ""
"in the worktree-specific (local) `.zed/tasks.json` file; such tasks are "
"available only when working on a project with that worktree included. You "
"can edit worktree-specific tasks by using the `zed: open project tasks` "
"action."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:76
msgid ""
"on the fly with [oneshot tasks](#oneshot-tasks). These tasks are project-"
"specific and do not persist across sessions."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:77
msgid "by language extension."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:79
msgid "Variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:81
msgid ""
"Zed tasks act just like your shell; that also means that you can reference "
"environmental variables via sh-esque `$VAR_NAME` syntax. A couple of "
"additional environmental variables are set for your convenience. These "
"variables allow you to pull information from the current editor and use it "
"in your tasks. The following variables are available:"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:84
msgid "`ZED_COLUMN`: current line column"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:85
msgid "`ZED_ROW`: current line row"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:86
msgid ""
"`ZED_FILE`: absolute path of the currently opened file (e.g. `/Users/my-user/"
"path/to/project/src/main.rs`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:87
msgid "`ZED_FILENAME`: filename of the currently opened file (e.g. `main.rs`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:88
msgid ""
"`ZED_DIRNAME`: absolute path of the currently opened file with file name "
"stripped (e.g. `/Users/my-user/path/to/project/src`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:89
msgid ""
"`ZED_RELATIVE_FILE`: path of the currently opened file, relative to "
"`ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT` (e.g. `src/main.rs`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:90
msgid ""
"`ZED_RELATIVE_DIR`: path of the currently opened file's directory, relative "
"to `ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT` (e.g. `src`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:91
msgid ""
"`ZED_STEM`: stem (filename without extension) of the currently opened file "
"(e.g. `main`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:92
msgid ""
"`ZED_SYMBOL`: currently selected symbol; should match the last symbol shown "
"in a symbol breadcrumb (e.g. `mod tests > fn test_task_contexts`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:93
msgid "`ZED_SELECTED_TEXT`: currently selected text"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:94
msgid ""
"`ZED_LANGUAGE`: language of the currently opened buffer (e.g. `Rust`, "
"`Python`, `Shell Script`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:95
msgid ""
"`ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT`: absolute path to the root of the current worktree. (e."
"g. `/Users/my-user/path/to/project`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:96
msgid ""
"`ZED_MAIN_GIT_WORKTREE`: absolute path to the main git worktree's working "
"directory. For normal checkouts this equals `ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT`; for linked "
"git worktrees this is the original repository's working directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:97
msgid ""
"`ZED_CUSTOM_RUST_PACKAGE`: (Rust-specific) name of the parent package of "
"$ZED_FILE source file."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:99
msgid "To use a variable in a task, prefix it with a dollar sign (`$`):"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:103 src/tasks.md:201 src/tasks.md:296
msgid "\"echo current file's path\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:104 src/tasks.md:297
msgid "\"echo $ZED_FILE\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:108
msgid ""
"You can also use verbose syntax that allows specifying a default if a given "
"variable is not available: `${ZED_FILE:default_value}`"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:110
msgid ""
"These environmental variables can also be used in tasks' `cwd`, `args`, and "
"`label` fields."
msgstr ""

