#: src/tasks.md:230
msgid "Hooks"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:232
msgid ""
"In addition to being spawned manually, tasks can be configured to run "
"automatically in response to certain Zed events by adding a hook to the "
"`hooks` field on a task template. A task with a matching hook will be "
"resolved and spawned when that event fires."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:234
msgid "The following hooks are currently supported:"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:236
msgid ""
"`create_worktree` — runs after Zed creates a new linked Git worktree, either "
"directly through the CLI or through the UI with the worktree modal. The task "
"is spawned with `ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT` pointing at the newly created worktree "
"and `ZED_MAIN_GIT_WORKTREE` pointing at the original repository's working "
"directory, which makes these hooks well-suited to copying untracked files "
"(such as `.env` files) or running per-worktree setup commands."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:238
msgid ""
"Hook tasks are resolved from the same global and worktree-local `tasks.json` "
"files as manually spawned tasks, and multiple tasks may register for the "
"same hook; they all run when the hook fires. A hook task still benefits from "
"the usual task configuration fields — `cwd`, `env`, `reveal`, `hide`, and so "
"on — so you can control how much of the terminal UI is shown while it runs."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:243
msgid "\"copy .env into new worktree\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:244
msgid "\"cp\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:245
msgid "\"$ZED_MAIN_GIT_WORKTREE/.env\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:245
msgid "\"$ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT/.env\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:246
msgid "\"hooks\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:246
msgid "\"create_worktree\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:247
msgid "\"reveal\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:247
msgid "\"no_focus\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:248
msgid "\"hide\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:248
msgid "\"on_success\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:253
msgid ""
"Tasks that define `hooks` are still available from the task modal like any "
"other task, so the same template can be reused for manual runs."
msgstr ""

